## Executive synopsis

You now hold a **12-billion-parameter, instruction-tuned, fully-multimodal Gemma-3 checkpoint** whose transformer layers were converted to **Torch-AO weight-only INT4 (group = 128)** while **SigLIP + mm-projection** remain in BF16.

* Disk: 8.1 GB (`pytorch_model-00001/2.bin`)
* RAM during quant.: 13 GB, wall-time ≈ 36 s
* Runtime VRAM need (TP = 2): ≈ 11.7 GB per RTX 3060 for LLM + 0.4 GB on GPU 0 for SigLIP; fits both cards with 0.6 GB head-room for KV-cache. ([huggingface.co][1], [github.com][2])

vLLM 0.9.x natively recognises Torch-AO INT4 tensors, routes image blobs through SigLIP, and serves an OpenAI-compatible API; only `--trust-remote-code` and correct TP size are required. ([huggingface.co][3], [docs.vllm.ai][4])

