## 2 Serving in vLLM 0.9

### 2.1  Launch command (dual RTX 3060)

```bash
pip install -U "vllm>=0.9.0" torch==2.5.0+cu121 --extra-index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu121

VLLM_USE_V1=1 vllm serve ./gemma-3-12b-it-int4wo-128 \
  --dtype bfloat16 \
  --tensor-parallel-size 2 \
  --max-model-len 4096 \
  --trust-remote-code \
  --limit-mm-per-prompt '{"image":2}'
```

* **`VLLM_USE_V1=1`** enables the new CUDA-graph attention engine (15-25 % boost). ([github.com][8])
* **`--dtype bfloat16`** leaves activations in BF16; INT4 tensors de-quantise on the fly.
* **`--limit-mm-per-prompt`** caps SigLIP token expansion; 2 images ≈ 512 extra tokens. ([docs.vllm.ai][4])
* **VRAM footprint** verified by community run on two 12 GB cards. ([huggingface.co][9])

### 2.2  OpenAI-style client snippet

```python
from openai import OpenAI, AsyncOpenAI
import base64, requests, json, os
os.environ["OPENAI_API_KEY"] = "none"
client = OpenAI(base_url="http://localhost:8000/v1")

b64 = base64.b64encode(open("dog.png","rb").read()).decode()
resp = client.chat.completions.create(
  model = "gemma-3-12b-it-int4",
  messages=[{
     "role":"user",
     "content":[
        {"type":"image_url",
         "image_url":{"url":f"data:image/png;base64,{b64}"}},
        {"type":"text","text":"What breed and colour is this dog?"}
     ]}],
  max_tokens=128)
print(resp.choices[0].message.content)
```

Schema identical to vLLM multimodal docs. ([docs.vllm.ai][10])

